@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Re-capture overwrites the stored range
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Child or grown-up" as user
box "Frontend — TwinkleTune web app" #E0F2FE
  participant "Entry point (settings / home / me)" as entry
  participant "routes['voice']" as router
  participant "renderVoiceSetup" as screen
  participant "store" as store
end box

user -> entry : Tap "Re-do" / voice card / "Find your voice"
note over entry : Three entry points: Grown-Ups Corner, home, Me screen (VP-L2-13)
entry -> router : location.hash = "#/voice"
router -> screen : renderVoiceSetup(root)
user -> screen : Complete capture with a new low and high
screen -> store : store.update overwrites profile.range = {low, high} (VP-L2-13)
note over store : Existing range replaced; later play uses the new shift (VP-L2-13)
screen --> user : Completion modal "Your voice is found! 🎉"
note over screen : The same persist-and-push then runs (see persist-and-sync-range)
@enduml
